title: A contained atom can be thought of as a branch of its container.
pid: a0144ae1-a281-4c9f-9694-364188c4c369
body: |2-
  For instance, consider this four-atom tree:
  #+begin_example
  - humility
  -- Humility makes love better.
  --- <an illustration of how humility can make love better>
  --- <another such illustration>
  -- Humility interacts with courage.
  #+end_example
  Here 'humility makes love better' is a branch of 'humility'.

  Note that it could also be a branch of 'love'.
  This illustrates the sense in which
  trees in the web of words can overlap.
